{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_xoy6ublmsziy6zkbc2rdxwfawh2wvvjp2wkestdpwzpwu7o67viq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The complete C library in `c_src/` is translated to Rust.\n\n## What was translated\n\nThe library is **cJSON 1.7.19**. The C build globs all of `c_src/` (`cJSON.c` + `test.c`) into one shared object, exporting **80 symbols** — 79 `cJSON_*` functions (including `cJSON_Duplicate_rec`, which is public in the `.c` but *not* in the header) plus `driver` from `test.c`.\n\n**Files written (in the current directory, not `c_src/`):**\n| File | Lines | Contents |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Cargo.toml` | — | `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]` |\n| `src/lib.rs` | 3258 | All of `cJSON.c` |\n| `src/test_driver.rs` | 235 | All of `test.c` (`driver`, `print_preallocated`, `create_objects`) |\n| `src/ffi.rs` | 58 | libc bindings |\n\n## Completion gate — symbol diff is empty\n\n```\nnm -D C .so:  80 symbols\nnm -D Rust .so: 80 symbols\ncomm -23 (missing from Rust): <empty>\ncomm -13 (extra in Rust):     <empty>\n```\nSymbol **types** (`T`/`D`) also match exactly, and the Rust `.so` needs only `libc`/`libgcc_s`/`ld-linux`.\n\n## Byte-identical output verified against the real C `.so`\n\nFour C harnesses were compiled twice — once linked to `libcjson_c.so`, once to the Rust `libcjson.so` — and outputs diffed:\n\n- **h1** (228 lines): `driver()`, 30 parse scenarios (BOM, malformed, surrogates, `\\u0000`, nesting), `end`/`GetErrorPtr` offsets, `Duplicate`, `Compare`, `PrintBuffered`, 24 number edge cases (NaN, ±inf, `DBL_MAX`, INT saturation) → **identical**\n- **h2** (113 lines): every add/create/detach/insert/replace/delete/predicate/reference API, `SetValuestring`, `SetNumberHelper`, all header macros, `Minify`, `PrintPreallocated` failure paths, custom hooks → **identical**\n- **hooks**: `InitHooks` with real `malloc`/`free` (enables the realloc path) vs. partial vs. wrapper hooks → **identical**\n- **fuzz**: 4000 randomly-assembled inputs (5139 lines / 347 KB of output) → **identical**, and re-run under `de_DE.utf8`, `fr_FR.utf8`, `C`, `POSIX` (decimal point `,` vs `.`) → **identical**\n\n## Fidelity notes\n\n- Numeric formatting delegates to C `snprintf`/`sscanf`/`strtod` and `localeconv()`, so `%1.15g`/`%1.17g` round-tripping and locale decimal points match bit-for-bit; `printf` is used in `driver` so stdout buffering/interleaving is unchanged.\n- Allocation uses libc `malloc`/`free`/`realloc` directly, so callers can still `free()` results of `cJSON_Print`.\n- `goto fail`/`goto success` became labeled blocks; original quirks were **preserved, not fixed** — e.g. `parse_string`'s fail path advancing `offset` past the opening quote, `parse_array` dereferencing before a bounds check, `cJSON_GetArraySize`'s `size_t`→`int` truncation, and the `(int)NaN` cast (reproduced as `INT_MIN`, matching x86-64 `cvttsd2si`, rather than Rust's saturating `0`).\n- `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] extern \"C\"` on every public function; no source-level namespace/renaming macros exist in this header (`CJSON_PUBLIC(x)` only adds a visibility attribute), so linker names equal source names — confirmed by the empty `nm` diff.\n\n`c_src/` is unmodified (MD5s recorded above). `cargo build --release` compiles clean with zero warnings."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1062,"cache_read_input_tokens":170370,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1062,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5d899639-f368-45e2-903f-34e2e514eda3","uuid":"ff6b61ad-102f-4e4a-a617-d2276f50396b","timestamp":"2026-08-20T02:45:28.936Z"}
